    {
      "id": "67fdce5f14afb8b8f358c81914176af53006b309",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3220210199,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I have to say, I am getting the idea of these changes, but I am questioning the approach a bit. Creating small classes just to overwrite one or two lines of text seems too intense for me. We should think to either make this json based, where we add a bunch of strings and settings that are app-specific to json files and compile them in a resource package (to make those translatable, you could take a look at how I did that for the slides.json files in CMakeLists.txt), or one super-class to handle most of the strings. We really should rethink this approach for 5.x though.\n\nI have removed the welcome_page for Stratoshark again btw, as with the recent changes from me (latest being the Update reminder) basically the class was empty. My comment is more targeted for the rest of these changes.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-04-03T14:29:35.534Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-03T14:57:02.170Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 443386118,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 22994,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3220265007,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I will suggest having all info banner content in a `.json` file (also the image, to make it simpler) and have only generic code to handle them. Then Stratoshark can be shipped with different .json files than Wireshark.",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/905aafc6b50e246885f5ea9273a9dc4f22e2658b71f9a1b551b797082bec3f80?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/stigbjorlykke"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-04-03T14:57:02.061Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-03T15:40:03.290Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 443386118,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 22994,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3220370552,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The goal here (and with related changes) is just to remove application_flavor_is_wireshark(), so developers aren't tempted to continue to use it as that is not \"generic UI\" for the applications we want to support.  Polymorphism has been the \"quickest\" way (for me). If UI dialogs can really get around all of the \"if application check\" strings with different JSON files (or application specific .ui files), that approach is fine with me.  You can also @ me for MRs that use that approach (as I learn how to do it)",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-04-03T15:51:48.801Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-03T15:51:48.801Z",
